SupraLINUX activity manager integration

Build the unchanged official stable daemon, its private plugin library, all seven
plugins, activation/systemd user files, KRunner metadata and translations.
Retain Ubuntu Qt and the SQLite runtime provider. No public SDK is introduced.
No upstream CTest suite is defined by this source.
The shared runner transports the complete hash-verified tests tree; the setup
references its sibling client files instead of embedding another copy.
The fixture uses a bounded private D-Bus with no service activation and disposable
HOME/XDG state. The actual installed daemon serves a client compiled against the
Ubuntu Plasma Activities SDK. Check offline rejected futures, create/rename/select
and restore signals/futures, C++/QML models, real SQLite resource link/unlink and
persistence after a daemon restart. Wait for the documented delayed config flush
before stopping the first daemon. Inspect actual SQLite integrity/schema and
link cleanup read-only; preserve original logs, including unavailable private
kglobalaccel activation. Stop only the owned daemon and bus, then remove private
configuration. Keep the Ubuntu client bytes and Activities/Qt runtime versions
across the candidate upgrade; rebuild a consumer against the current test inputs.
Actual desktop global shortcuts, application/event spying, KRunner activation and
full session integration remain later functional gates.
